              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "If you are looking for free satellite radio, the options depend on whether you want a truly free subscription, a temporary trial, or a free alternative that feels like satellite radio. \n\nSince **SiriusXM** is the only major satellite radio provider in North America, most \"free\" satellite radio options revolve around their services and promotions. \n\n---\n\n### 1. SiriusXM\u2019s \"Free Access\" Plan (Ad-Supported)\nSiriusXM offers a **Free Access Plan**\u2014a completely free, ad-supported tier designed for inactive in-car radios. \n* **How it works:** You get dozens of popular music, news, talk, and sports channels (including *SiriusXM Hits 1*, *'90s on 9*, *Alt Nation*, and *ESPN Radio*) directly through your car\u2019s dashboard. \n* **The Catch:** \n  * **No credit card is required**, but it is **only available on newer vehicles** equipped with SiriusXM's **360L hybrid radios** (typically 2023 or newer models from manufacturers like Ford, GM, Subaru, Dodge, and Nissan).\n  * It is **in-car only**. It does not include access to the SiriusXM mobile app.\n  * **The 60-Day Rule:** To keep the service active, you must use it at least once every 60 days. If you don't, the plan is deactivated.\n  * It is currently only offered in the United States (SiriusXM Canada does not offer this tier).\n\n### 2. SiriusXM Free Trials & Promotional Events\nIf your vehicle doesn't qualify for the Free Access Plan, you can still get SiriusXM for free temporarily using these methods:\n* **In-Car Free Trials:** If you buy a new or certified pre-owned vehicle with a factory-installed satellite radio, it almost always comes with a **3-month free trial** of the Platinum plan. No credit card is required to start this trial, and it automatically shuts off when it's over. \n* **Streaming-Only Trials:** SiriusXM frequently offers 1- to 3-month free trials of their streaming app for new customers. *Note: These usually require a credit card and will auto-renew at the standard monthly rate if you don\u2019t cancel before the trial ends.*\n* **Carrier and Brand Perks:** Mobile carriers and device brands often bundle free SiriusXM streaming. For example, T-Mobile has historically offered several months \"On Us\", and Samsung occasionally runs 6-month free streaming trials through the Galaxy Store.\n* **Free Listening Events:** A few times a year (typically around major US holidays like Memorial Day, Thanksgiving, or Labor Day), SiriusXM will temporarily **unlock inactive satellite radios** for a week or two. During these \"Free Listening\" events, you can just turn on your car radio and start listening to selected channels without signing up for anything.\n\n### 3. Free Internet Radio Alternatives (App-Based)\nIf you want the variety and curation of satellite radio without paying a subscription, many free, ad-supported internet radio services offer a nearly identical experience. While they rely on your phone\u2019s cell data or Wi-Fi rather than a direct satellite feed, they are highly popular alternatives:\n* **TuneIn:** Gives you access to thousands of live local AM/FM stations, global news networks, podcasts, and sports. \n* **iHeartRadio:** Features thousands of live radio stations across the country, custom artist-themed stations, and a massive podcast library.\n* **Pandora:** Owned by SiriusXM, Pandora lets you create free, ad-supported custom stations based on your favorite artists or genres.\n* **Radio Garden:** A unique, free app that allows you to rotate a 3D globe and tune into thousands of live, local radio stations broadcasting across the world in real-time.\n\n### 4. Free-to-Air (FTA) Satellite Radio (For Hobbyists)\nIf you are a tech hobbyist and want actual satellite-beamed radio without paying a company, you can look into **Free-To-Air (FTA) Satellite**. \nBy purchasing a satellite dish (C-band or Ku-band) and a DVB satellite receiver, you can tune into hundreds of unencrypted, free radio stations broadcast over the air via satellite. However, this requires significant physical setup, and you will not get premium commercial networks like SiriusXM.",
